  - "reproducible research"
abstract: >-
  This repository contains a TEMOA 3.0 capacity expansion model of the
  Shungnak community energy system in rural Alaska. It represents electricity
  demand, diesel generation, solar photovoltaic generation, distributed wind,
  small hydropower, and battery storage from 2025 through 2045. The repository
  includes six planning scenarios, version controlled SQL inputs, archived
  reference results, parameter provenance, and scripts for rebuilding,
  solving, exporting, testing, and scientifically verifying the TEMOA
  planning results. The separate rolling horizon unit commitment model used
  in the associated study is outside the scope of this repository.
